{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Concerning his son.</b> Meaning: lest he go out into bad society and become sunk in evil beliefs when he leaves his father's house, and in the end he is ultimately his son." "It further intends <b>concerning his son</b> — that Sarah attributed him to Hagar, as she said: ״הָאָמָה וְאֶת בְּנָהּ וְגוֹ׳ בֶּן הָאָמָה״ (the maidservant and her son… the son of the maidservant). And the Holy One, blessed be He, came and justified Sarah's words and said to him: ״כָּל אֲשֶׁר וְגוֹ׳ שְׁמַע בְּקוֹלָהּ״ (all that… hearken to her voice), and do not consider him your son. And this is what it says <b>concerning the lad</b> etc. — He removed from him the name of son and said to him: ״כִּי בְיִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ״ וְגוֹ׳ (for in Isaac shall seed be called to you), but this son shall be called after the name of his mother, as it says <b>וְגַם אֶת בֶּן הָאָמָה</b> etc. (and also the son of the maidservant). And you will find that Abraham turned and acknowledged her words, for it is written: ״וַיַּשְׁכֵּם אַבְרָהָם וְגוֹ׳ וְאֶת הַיֶּלֶד״ וְגוֹ׳ (And Abraham rose early… and the lad), and he did not say ״וְאֶת בְּנוֹ״ (and his son), for Scripture testified concerning Abraham."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:39.809898383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}